# Your own ignores go ABOVE the marker below, and stay there across upgrades.
# Everything from the marker down is replaced wholesale when the template is upgraded; anything
# you write below it is lost. Nothing above it is ever touched.
#
# The order is not cosmetic. .gitignore resolves last-match-wins, so upstream's patterns sit at
# the bottom deliberately: a `!negation` written up here cannot silently re-admit a file the
# never-commit list excludes. That is the one thing this layout is protecting.

# Python / uv — delete this block if the project is not Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/


# ─── UPSTREAM BLOCK — rnd-project-memory; replaced on upgrade, do not edit below ───

# Never commit — see ai-sandbox/SOURCES.md
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
data/

# Extracted data, in any of its usual shapes
*.csv
*.parquet
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.xlsx
*.feather
*.h5

# Backstop only. reference-only sources are NEVER placed in the repository
# (ai-sandbox/SOURCES.md); this line exists to catch the mistake, not to
# sanction the directory.
sources/reference-only/
